# Integer8 literal above the maximum

Verifies an int8 literal one past the 8-bit maximum is rejected with a
compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
too_large: int8 = 128
print(too_large)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `128` for type `int8`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 18, end: 21 }

<<< exit
1
